Z||000020||mwbackus||05-13-2000||04:46 PM||||Just had a question:<P>With all of the "Free" ISP's available now, why do you still use AOL?  Are there any other benefits such as the instant messaging that keep you with the AOL service?<P>Mike B.||||reg||1
Z||000021||TheFiero64||05-13-2000||05:22 PM||||You can use <B>AOL Instant Messenger</B> FREE without having aol. I use Mediaone which is more money than AOL, but is a cable modem connection which is much much faster than a 56K hookup!||||reg||10
Z||000022||Jaygee79||05-13-2000||05:40 PM||||Actually, there are many benefits to having AOL.  I would be lost without it.  There's a free calendar that you can organize your appointments on, there's free games that only AOL members have access to, websites that only AOL members have access to, a picture service where you can have your pics sent to your email address instead of having to pick them up, chat rooms for AOL members only, a free reminder service for birthdays, holidays, etc. sent to you, and more that I can't think of right now.  It's totally worth the money.||||reg||7
Z||000023||Dan86gt3.8||05-13-2000||09:20 PM||||well yeah I have seen thoose free ip's half the screen covered with ads. and it kicks you off if you don't click on one of them within 10 minutes, yeah sounds like something I want. besides I like aol, I like the email and internet and chat all in one thing.  I hate having to go to a site and login to read mail, and everytime you read or respond you have to wait for a page to load, etc, etc.  I dunoo its just conveniet and works real well with a my parents new computer.  call me lazy but its just to easy to change||||reg||1
Z||000024||mwbackus||05-14-2000||12:08 AM||||I use a free isp, it works better than any other dial-up isp account I have used including USWest, MCI, AT&T, Local ISP's, UUNET, etc.  There are no advertisements: if you know the tricks to set it up, it works just like any dial-up.  I really dont think that any "modem" line is worth paying for, just wanted to know if there was some reason that so many people still use a service like AOL.  If anyone here on the forum is interested in an alternative to throwing away $20 a month, I would be happy to help.<P>Mike B.||||reg||1
